  ex:"This checks <b>mature judgment</b>: microservices are not always better. Monoliths are simpler to build, deploy, and debug. Microservices give independent scaling and deployment but bring network failures, harder debugging, and data consistency problems. <b>Sync</b> = REST/gRPC (simple, but it couples services). <b>Async</b> = events through Kafka (decoupled, eventually consistent). The <b>Saga</b> pattern handles transactions across services: each service does its local step, and if a later step fails, <b>compensating actions</b> undo the earlier ones.",
